---
title: How to Use Reports
description: >-
  Open a report, choose a period, narrow it to one client or team member, save
  the ones you use often, and export them to CSV.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---
**Reports answers questions about your projects, clients, invoices and team in one place. Pick a report, choose a period, then save it or export it.**

### **Who Can Open It**

Reports is part of the **Reports & Analytics** feature of your plan.

- **Administrators and Managers** can open it by default.
- Other roles need an administrator to give them access.

**Navigation:** Administrative → **Reports** (or go to `/reports`).

### **Open a Report**

1. Open **Reports**. The list of reports is on the left.
2. Find a report. Click a category such as **Projects** or **Finance** to open it, or type in **Search reports** to search every category at once.
3. Click the report name. It opens on the right with charts and tables.
4. Click the arrow at the top of the list to collapse it when you want more room.

### **Choose a Period**

Every report has a period menu: **Always**, **Today**, **This Week**, **This Month**, **This Year** or **Custom Range**. **Always** covers everything up to today. For a custom range, enter the start and end dates and click **Apply**.

The project reports count a project in the period it was created, so use **Always** or a wide range when you look at older projects. Each report opens on the period that suits it best. Revenue reports open on **This Month** and recurring revenue opens on **This Year**, for example.

### **Narrow a Report**

Some reports have pickers inside the report:

- **Project reports** (Project Health, Task Completion, Time Tracking, Resource Utilization, Member Performance and Project Overview) can be narrowed by **Client**, **Program** and **Category**. Use them together to answer a question like "how are all my SEO projects doing?". When you pick more than one, a project must match all of them.
- **Support Overview** has client and team member pickers.
- The client reports, such as **Client Time Report** and **Company Overview**, have client and company pickers.

Clear a picker to see everyone again. A picker applies to the report you are viewing and is not kept when you open another report. Exporting to CSV keeps the pickers you chose.

**Project Overview** and **Project Health** also show a **By Program** and a **By Category** table, with the number of projects per group by status. Projects without a program or category are grouped as **No program** and **No category**. A project that is in several categories is counted once in each of them.

### **Save a Report**

1. Open the report and set its period.
2. Click **Save**.
3. Enter a **Report Name** (for example "Q1 2026 Revenue") and an optional description.
4. Tick the pin option to keep it at the top of your saved reports.

A saved report remembers the report and its period, including a custom date range. It does not remember a client or team member picker, so choose those again after you open it.

Saved reports are listed under **Saved Reports** in the sidebar, pinned ones first. Click **Run** to open one, or **Delete** to remove it.

### **Export to CSV**

Click **Export CSV** to download the report you are viewing as a spreadsheet file, for the period shown.

### **Which Report Answers Which Question**

| Category | Reports | Use it to |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Projects | Project Health, Task Completion, Time Tracking, Resource Utilization, Project–Client Summary, Milestone Tracker, Member Performance, Client Project Summary, Project Overview | See which projects are late, who is overloaded, where hours went, and how each client's projects are doing. Project Overview combines most of these in one page. |
| Team | Member Activity Summary, Member Deal Performance, Member Lead Performance, Member Project & Task Breakdown | See what each person works on and delivers across the workspace. |
| Finance | Revenue Summary, Invoice Summary, Recurring Revenue, Payment Gateway Performance, Tax Report, Discount & Coupon Impact, Quotation Funnel, Outstanding Invoices, Cash Flow | Follow money in and out, unpaid invoices by age, and tax collected. |
| Invoice | Invoice Overview, Monthly Revenue Trend, Collection Rate & Pending, Refund & Void Invoices, Client Lifetime Invoice Value | Track collections, 12-month trends and value per client. |
| Leads | Lead Funnel, Lead Source ROI, Lead Aging, Lead Group Performance | Find the sources that bring the best leads and the leads going stale. |
| Deals | Deal Pipeline, Deal Forecast, Deal Activity Log | See win and loss rates, expected revenue and the most active deals. |
| Clients | Client Activity, Customer Lifetime Value, Company Overview, Geographic Distribution, Engagement Score, Client Portal Engagement, Client Time Report | Understand each client's value, activity and the time spent on them. |
| Support | Support Tickets, Open vs Close Rate, Agent Performance, Ticket Activity, Ticket Backlog & Aging, Client Ticket Summary, Support Overview, SLA Report | Watch ticket volume, response times and SLA compliance. |
| Other modules | Service Catalog, Meetings, Emails Inbox, WhatsApp, Forms, Documents, Automation | Orders and revenue per service, bookings, email delivery, conversations, form submissions, signatures and workflow runs. |

See also [How to Use the Profit Tracker](/project-management/how-to-use-the-profit-tracker/) for revenue, cost and profit per project.
